# AGENTS.md

Owned by the project team. Tells the SDD harness and AI agents how to work in this repository.
Fill in the sections below; the `## Stack` section is mandatory.

## Stack

- Backend: PHP >= 8.2, Laravel, database (PostgreSQL/MySQL/SQLite)
- Frontend: React (Vite + TypeScript) | VueJs (Vite + TypeScript)
- Backend tests: Pest | PHPUnit
- Frontend tests: Vitest + Testing Library | Playwright (e2e)

## Commands

- Backend run: `php artisan serve`
- Backend tests: `vendor/bin/pest` | `php artisan test`
- Frontend run: `npm run dev`
- Frontend tests: `npm run test`
- Lint: `vendor/bin/pint`, `npm run lint`

## Git

- Repo topology: `single-repo` | `multirepo (human-managed)` (set by `/sdd-init`
  via `detect_repo_topology.py` and confirmed with the human).
- `single-repo`: the project root is its own git work tree; the SDD agent drives
  atomic Conventional Commits per task (`check_commit.py`).
- `multirepo`: the human owns all git operations. The agent never runs git write
  commands (add/commit/branch/checkout/push/pull/merge/stash/rebase/reset/tag/worktree);
  it implements in the working tree, runs the gates, and hands a commit-ready
  summary to the human. Read-only git (status/diff/log) is always allowed.

## Conventions

- Backend code lives in `app/` (controllers, services, models, migrations, tests).
- Frontend code lives in `resources/js/` or a dedicated frontend package.
- One commit per task; tests must pass before a task is marked DONE.
- API responses follow Laravel resource conventions; errors use JSON structure.
